{"step_index":11,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T08:33:53Z","content":"--- **SURGERY I MOST IMPORTANT TOPICS** --- **UNIT 6 NEUROSURGERY 18 percent / 10 hrs** Very high priority for Endsem **Must do** 1 Craniotomy indications types steps complications 2 Decompressive craniectomy in TBI 3 Laminectomy indications procedure complications 4 Aneurysm clipping vs coiling 5 Stereotactic surgery 6 Deep Brain Stimulation DBS 7 Rhizotomy 8 Thalamotomy 9 Neural implants 10 Postoperative management/physiotherapy after neurosurgery **Most likely long questions** • Craniotomy • Decompressive craniectomy • Laminectomy • Aneurysm clipping/coiling --- **UNIT 2 INFECTIONS and POST OPERATIVE CARE 21 percent / 12 hrs** Highest weightage overall **Must do** 1 Surgical infections classification 2 Cellulitis 3 Abscess 4 Gangrene types and management 5 Tuberculosis 6 Hospital acquired infections 7 Postoperative complications • Shock • DVT • Wound infection • Atelectasis • Pneumonia • UTI • Pressure sores 8 Physiotherapy management after surgery 9 DVT signs prevention and management 10 Wound infection and wound healing **Very important** Postoperative complications and physiotherapy implications --- **UNIT 3 ONCOLOGY AMPUTATION and VASCULAR 14 percent / 8 hrs** Endsem HIGH PRIORITY **Oncology** • Cancer definition and staging • Principles of cancer treatment • Surgery/radiotherapy/chemotherapy • Mastectomy • Complications after mastectomy • Physiotherapy after mastectomy **Amputation** • Indications • Levels of amputation • Complications • Stump care • Phantom limb • Prosthetic rehabilitation • Cineplasty **Vascular** • Varicose veins • Peripheral arterial occlusive disease • DVT • Surgical management of vascular disorders **Very likely** Mastectomy amputation PAOD varicose veins --- **UNIT 1 SURGICAL PRINCIPLES 20 percent / 11 hrs** Highest weightage and Midsem **Must do** **Wound** • Wound healing • Factors affecting wound healing • Type